{"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":5,"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"name":"python3","display_name":"Python 3","language":"python"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.12"},"ground_truth_ml":{"edition":"propensity-4.0","execution_order":["01_data_readiness_and_eda","02_basic_modeling","03_advanced_modeling","04_member_scoring_and_business_decision"],"requires_prior_outputs":false,"student_package":{"course_id":"ground-truth-gym-l3-4.0","setup_cell_added":true,"original_lesson_code_unchanged":true}}},"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"course-start-guide","metadata":{},"source":["## Start here — Google Colab\n\nOpen this notebook from the course website or GitHub. On first use, the setup cell connects Google Drive and places the public course folder there if it is not already present. It expands the prepared synthetic inputs and installs the pinned libraries automatically.\n\nStart with **01** and run each notebook in order: **01 → 02 → 03 → 04**. Keep the course folder together and use the same Colab runtime for the sequence. CPU is sufficient. The data-generation notebook is not part of this learner path."]},{"cell_type":"code","id":"course-auto-setup","metadata":{"tags":["course-setup"]},"source":["# Connect Drive and prepare this course automatically before importing lesson libraries.\n","from pathlib import Path\n","import gzip\n","import os\n","import shutil\n","import sys\n","import json\n","import subprocess\n","import importlib.metadata as package_metadata\n","\n","COURSE_ID = 'ground-truth-gym-l3-4.0'\n","MARKER = 'COURSE_PACKAGE.json'\n","REPOSITORY_URL = 'https://github.com/GroundTruthML/Course_Material.git'\n","REPOSITORY_FOLDER = 'GroundTruth_Course_Material'\n","try:\n","    from google.colab import drive\n","except ImportError:\n","    drive = None\n","\n","if drive is not None:\n","    drive.mount('/content/drive')\n","    search_root = Path('/content/drive/MyDrive')\n","else:\n","    search_root = Path.cwd()\n","\n","\n","def is_course_folder(path):\n","    marker = path / MARKER\n","    return marker.is_file() and json.loads(marker.read_text()).get('course_id') == COURSE_ID\n","\n","\n","def find_local_course():\n","    for candidate in [Path.cwd(), *Path.cwd().parents]:\n","        if is_course_folder(candidate):\n","            return candidate\n","    return None\n","\n","\n","def find_drive_course(root):\n","    matches = []\n","    for directory, subfolders, files in os.walk(root):\n","        subfolders[:] = [name for name in subfolders if not name.startswith('.') and name not in {'node_modules', '__pycache__', '.git'}]\n","        if MARKER in files:\n","            candidate = Path(directory)\n","            if is_course_folder(candidate):\n","                matches.append(candidate)\n","                subfolders[:] = []\n","    canonical = root / REPOSITORY_FOLDER / 'course_material' / 'gym'\n","    if is_course_folder(canonical):\n","        return canonical\n","    if len(matches) == 1:\n","        return matches[0]\n","    if len(matches) > 1:\n","        raise RuntimeError('More than one Gym course folder was found in My Drive. Keep one copy, then rerun this cell.')\n","    return None\n","\n","\n","course_root = find_drive_course(search_root) if drive is not None else find_local_course()\n","if course_root is None and drive is not None:\n","    repository_root = search_root / REPOSITORY_FOLDER\n","    if repository_root.exists():\n","        raise RuntimeError('The course repository folder exists but is incomplete. Remove that incomplete copy from My Drive and rerun this cell.')\n","    subprocess.check_call(['git', 'clone', '--depth', '1', REPOSITORY_URL, str(repository_root)])\n","    course_root = repository_root / 'course_material' / 'gym'\n","if course_root is None or not is_course_folder(course_root):\n","    raise RuntimeError('Open this notebook from the public Course_Material repository, or keep the complete course_material/gym folder together.')\n","os.chdir(course_root)\n","\n","# Expand only the prepared synthetic input files. Notebook outputs are written separately.\n","DATA_DIR = course_root / 'gym_case_data'\n","INPUT_DIR = course_root / 'input_data' / 'gym_case_data'\n","if not (DATA_DIR / 'manifest.json').exists():\n","    shutil.copy2(INPUT_DIR / 'manifest.json', DATA_DIR / 'manifest.json')\n","manifest = json.loads((DATA_DIR / 'manifest.json').read_text())\n","(DATA_DIR / 'raw').mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n","for table_name in manifest['tables']:\n","    csv_path = DATA_DIR / 'raw' / f'{table_name}.csv'\n","    if not csv_path.exists():\n","        compressed_path = INPUT_DIR / 'raw' / f'{table_name}.csv.gz'\n","        if not compressed_path.exists():\n","            raise FileNotFoundError(f'Missing prepared input: {compressed_path}')\n","        with gzip.open(compressed_path, 'rb') as source, csv_path.open('wb') as destination:\n","            shutil.copyfileobj(source, destination)\n","\n","requirements = (course_root / 'requirements-colab.txt').read_text().splitlines()\n","requirements = [line.strip() for line in requirements if line.strip() and not line.startswith('#')]\n","if drive is not None:\n","    dependency_dir = Path('/content/groundtruth_gym_dependencies')\n","    stamp = dependency_dir / 'course_requirements.json'\n","    if not stamp.exists() or json.loads(stamp.read_text()) != requirements:\n","        subprocess.check_call([sys.executable, '-m', 'pip', 'install', '--quiet', '--upgrade', '--target', str(dependency_dir), *requirements])\n","        stamp.write_text(json.dumps(requirements))\n","    sys.path.insert(0, str(dependency_dir))\n","    for distribution, module in [('numpy', 'numpy'), ('pandas', 'pandas'), ('scipy', 'scipy'), ('scikit-learn', 'sklearn'), ('matplotlib', 'matplotlib'), ('joblib', 'joblib')]:\n","        expected = next(line.split('==')[1] for line in requirements if line.startswith(distribution + '=='))\n","        loaded = sys.modules.get(module)\n","        if loaded is not None and getattr(loaded, '__version__', expected) != expected:\n","            raise RuntimeError('Please select Runtime > Disconnect and delete runtime, reconnect, and Run all. No path or package configuration is needed.')\n","\n","for item in requirements:\n","    distribution, expected = item.split('==')\n","    actual = package_metadata.version(distribution)\n","    if actual != expected:\n","        raise RuntimeError(f'{distribution}: expected {expected}, found {actual}. Use a fresh Colab runtime and run this first cell.')\n","\n","for variable in ['OMP_NUM_THREADS', 'OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS', 'MKL_NUM_THREADS']:\n","    os.environ[variable] = '1'\n","print('Course ready:', course_root)\n","print('Prepared synthetic inputs are ready. Run notebooks 01 → 02 → 03 → 04 in this order.')"],"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"section":""},"source":["# 02 — Basic modeling: build and compare a purchase ranking\n","\n","**Goal:** Use decision-time member information to rank future PT buyers, then compare the ranking with the staff rule.\n","\n","**Before you start:** Run notebook 01. Work from this Current folder with gym_case_data next to the notebook.\n","\n","| What goes in | What comes out |\n","|---|---|\n","| Clean activity/profile/store tables and decision-aligned observations | One member-level feature table |\n","| Complete January outcomes | Training-fitted Logistic and GBM pipelines |\n","| Complete February outcomes | A comparison at the promotion selection fraction |\n","| Fixed feature definitions and settings | A saved handoff for advanced modeling |\n","\n","### Follow the seven steps\n","\n","| Section | Main question |\n","|---|---|\n","| MOD-01 | What are X, y and the business decision? |\n","| MOD-02 | How do event rows become one member row? |\n","| MOD-03 | Which data learns, compares and evaluates? |\n","| MOD-04 | What does preprocessing do to a member? |\n","| MOD-05 | How do Logistic and GBM learn from the same inputs? |\n","| MOD-06 | Which method finds more buyers at the actual selection budget? |\n","| MOD-07 | What must be saved for the next notebook? |\n","\n","**Reading pattern:** Read the question and plan → run the annotated cell → inspect its output → read the takeaway.\n","\n","**Scope:** All eligible PT histories remain included. Scores estimate new purchase likelihood under historical conditions. Notebook 03 develops feature alternatives and evaluates April; this notebook compares the full-feature baselines on February."],"id":"02-000"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"section":"MOD-01 — Define what X, y and the decision mean"},"source":["## MOD-01 — Define what X, y and the decision mean\n","\n","### The question\n","What information should the model receive, and what should it predict?\n","\n","| Item | Definition in this case |\n","|---|---|\n","| **One observation** | One eligible member at one decision time |\n","| **X: model inputs** | 12 numeric + 6 categorical candidates known at that decision |\n","| **y=1** | A new valid PT package purchase in the following 30 days, reconciled at day 33 |\n","| **y=0** | Complete payment window with no qualifying new purchase |\n","| **Unknown y** | Pending or incomplete outcome; excluded from supervised fitting |\n","| **Business use** | Score 1,200 eligible members; business selects the top 1,000 |\n","\n","### What the next cell does\n","1. Imports the libraries and defines input/output paths.\n","2. Sets the fixed model parameters and the 5/6 promotion fraction.\n","3. Loads notebook 01's saved tables and defines the candidate feature contract.\n","\n","**Why these candidates?** EDA supports testing engagement, PT history, profile and store context together. This basic comparison starts with all 18 checked inputs.\n","\n","![Notebook02 candidate families](attachment:02_basic_modeling_01_feature_families.png)\n","\n","### What to look for\n","Inspect each feature's **source, time window and meaning**. Promotion and consultation records remain outside X; they explain operations rather than supply predictors."],"attachments":{"02_basic_modeling_01_feature_families.png":{"image/png":""}},"id":"02-001"},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"section":"MOD-01 — Define what X, y and the decision mean"},"source":["# Import libraries: file paths, tables, plots, model pipelines and saved artifacts.\n","from pathlib import Path\n","import json\n","import hashlib\n","import numpy as np\n","import pandas as pd\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","from IPython.display import display\n","from sklearn.base import clone\n","from sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\n","from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n","from sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\n","from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler, OneHotEncoder\n","from sklearn.ensemble import GradientBoostingClassifier\n","from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n","from sklearn.metrics import average_precision_score, brier_score_loss\n","import sklearn\n","import joblib\n","\n","\n","# Input and output paths: run from Current; notebook01 has already written these files.\n","DATA_DIR = Path('gym_case_data')\n","MODEL_DIR = DATA_DIR / 'model'\n","MODEL_DIR.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n","assert (DATA_DIR / 'observations.csv').exists(), 'Run notebook 01 first.'\n","manifest = json.loads((DATA_DIR / 'manifest.json').read_text())\n","\n","\n","# Reproducibility and business budget: seed fixes random choices;5/6 is the promotion fraction.\n","SEED = manifest['seed']\n","CONTACT_FRACTION = 5 / 6\n","\n","\n","# Logistic parameters: smaller C means stronger regularization; max_iter is the solver limit.\n","LOGISTIC_C = 0.3\n","MAX_ITERATIONS = 1000\n","\n","\n","# GBM parameters: limit the number, size and learning speed of the small trees.\n","GBM_TREES = 50\n","GBM_LEARNING_RATE = 0.05\n","GBM_MAX_DEPTH = 2\n","GBM_MIN_LEAF = 20\n","\n","\n","# Feature routing: measurements/counts go to the numeric transformer; labels/IDs stay outside X.\n","NUMERIC_FEATURES = ['tenure_days', 'checkins_30d', 'classes_30d', 'app_views_30d', 'days_since_checkin', 'inquiry_60d', 'checkins_7d', 'checkin_momentum', 'pt_sessions_30d', 'prior_pt_purchases', 'days_since_pt_purchase', 'remaining_pt_sessions']\n","\n","\n","# Categorical feature handling: these strings will be imputed and one-hot encoded later.\n","CATEGORICAL_FEATURES = ['plan_type', 'preferred_channel', 'acquisition_source', 'location_id', 'city', 'pt_relationship']\n","FEATURE_COLUMNS = NUMERIC_FEATURES + CATEGORICAL_FEATURES\n","print('[INFO]', {'data_version': manifest['data_version'], 'seed': SEED, 'contact_fraction': CONTACT_FRACTION,\n","                 'logistic_C': LOGISTIC_C, 'max_iterations': MAX_ITERATIONS,\n","                 'gbm_trees': GBM_TREES, 'gbm_min_leaf': GBM_MIN_LEAF})\n","\n","\n","# Load the observation table from01; parse timestamps into comparable UTC values.\n","observations = pd.read_csv(DATA_DIR / 'observations.csv')\n","for column in observations:\n","    if column.endswith('_at') or column in ['decision_time', 'outcome_end', 'payments_complete_through']:\n","        observations[column] = pd.to_datetime(observations[column], utc=True, format=\"mixed\")\n","\n","\n","# Load clean events; event_time and available_at support the two-clock feature cutoff.\n","activities = pd.read_csv(DATA_DIR / 'clean/activity_events.csv')\n","for column in ['event_time', 'available_at']:\n","    activities[column] = pd.to_datetime(activities[column], utc=True, format=\"mixed\")\n","\n","\n","# Store context is a static dimension in this synthetic fixture.\n","locations = pd.read_csv(DATA_DIR / 'clean/locations.csv')\n","\n","\n","# Feature definitions: document sources/windows before deriving measurements.\n","feature_contract = pd.DataFrame([\n","    ('tenure_days', 'member signup', 'known signup → decision', 'membership age in days'),\n","    ('checkins_30d', 'activity_events', '[decision − 30d, decision)', 'known check-in count'),\n","    ('classes_30d', 'activity_events', '[decision − 30d, decision)', 'known class count'),\n","    ('app_views_30d', 'activity_events', '[decision − 30d, decision)', 'known app-view count'),\n","    ('days_since_checkin', 'activity_events', 'supplied 90-day history', 'recency; missing if no known visit'),\n","    ('inquiry_60d', 'activity_events', '[decision − 60d, decision)', 'any known enquiry'),\n","    ('checkins_7d / checkin_momentum', 'activity_events', '7d versus preceding 23d', 'recent visits and difference in daily visit rates'),\n","    ('pt_sessions_30d', 'activity_events', '[decision - 30d, decision)', 'known recent PT attendance'),\n","    ('prior_pt_purchases / days_since_pt_purchase / remaining_pt_sessions', 'decision-time CRM snapshot', 'strictly pre-decision purchase history', 'prior purchase count, recency and remaining balance'),\n","    ('pt_relationship', 'decision-time CRM snapshot', 'at decision', 'never_pt, active_pt or lapsed_pt; no exclusion'),\n","    ('plan_type / preferred_channel / acquisition_source', 'member decision snapshot', 'at decision', 'string profile fields'),\n","    ('location_id / city', 'snapshot and location dimension', 'at decision', 'store context')],\n","    columns=['feature', 'source', 'window', 'meaning'])\n","\n","\n","# Inspect and save the contract so later notebooks can trace each input.\n","display(feature_contract)\n","feature_contract.to_csv(MODEL_DIR / 'feature_contract.csv', index=False)"],"execution_count":null,"outputs":[],"id":"02-002"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"section":"MOD-01 — Define what X, y and the decision mean"},"source":["### Takeaway — MOD-01\n","\n","**You now have a defined X/y contract and visible configuration.** Candidate inputs describe the member before the decision; the target describes a new purchase afterward.\n","\n","**Before moving on:** Explain in your own words how this output supports the next step."],"id":"02-003"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"section":"MOD-02 — Turn known event rows into one member row"},"source":["## MOD-02 — Turn known event rows into one member row\n","\n","### The question\n","How can many activity rows describe one member without multiplying the modeling examples?\n","\n","### The plan\n","- **Keep known events:** event_time < decision_time and available_at <= decision_time.\n","- **Summarize activity:** counts over 7/30 days, prior enquiry over 60 days, and visit recency from the supplied history.\n","- **Add context:** tenure and decision-time PT/profile facts, then the static fixture's store dimension.\n","- **Preserve the unit:** one member-decision row, with checked join cardinality.\n","\n","**Missing has meaning:** No known check-in gives missing visit recency. A never-buyer has no previous purchase date. Keep these cases for later imputation and missingness indicators.\n","\n","### What to look for\n","Compare the displayed raw events with the example feature row. Check the printed **row counts, unmatched identities and duplicate keys**. The event summary should explain the member's measurements."],"id":"02-004"},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"section":"MOD-02 — Turn known event rows into one member row"},"source":["# Keep decisions that have occurred by extraction; planned future decisions lack reconstructible history.\n","entered_observations = observations.loc[observations.decision_time.le(pd.Timestamp(manifest['extracted_at']))].copy()\n","print(f'[CHECK] Entered snapshot filter: {len(observations)} to {len(entered_observations)} members (dropped {len(observations)-len(entered_observations)} planned future decisions).')\n","\n","\n","# Aggregate one measurement dictionary per member; event rows do not become extra examples.\n","feature_rows = []\n","for number, member in enumerate(entered_observations.itertuples(index=False), start=1):\n","\n","    # Check that the profile snapshot and prior-history dates are valid at this decision.\n","    assert member.snapshot_available_at <= member.decision_time\n","    assert member.signup_at <= member.decision_time\n","    assert pd.isna(member.last_pt_purchase_at) or member.last_pt_purchase_at < member.decision_time\n","    assert member.eligible\n","\n","    # Profile and remaining-session values are fixture decision snapshots.\n","    # A real deployment requires effective-time/version history for each mutable field.\n","    # Find this member's events through the unique identity key.\n","    member_events = activities.loc[activities.uid.eq(member.uid)]\n","\n","    # Two clocks: occurrence before the decision AND source availability by the decision.\n","    known_events = member_events.loc[member_events.event_time.lt(member.decision_time)\n","                                     & member_events.available_at.le(member.decision_time)]\n","\n","    # Apply30-day and60-day windows only after removing unavailable/future events.\n","    recent_events = known_events.loc[known_events.event_time.ge(member.decision_time - pd.Timedelta(days=30))]\n","    checkins = known_events.loc[known_events.event_type.eq('checkin')]\n","    enquiries = known_events.loc[known_events.event_type.eq('pt_inquiry')\n","                                 & known_events.event_time.ge(member.decision_time - pd.Timedelta(days=60))]\n","\n","    # Short-term activity and momentum: compare last7-day rate with the preceding23-day rate.\n","    checkins_7d = int((checkins.event_time >= member.decision_time-pd.Timedelta(days=7)).sum())\n","    checkins_30d = int(recent_events.event_type.eq('checkin').sum())\n","\n","    # Build numeric features; missing recency stays NaN when no relevant prior event exists.\n","    feature_rows.append({'checkins_7d': checkins_7d,\n","                         'checkin_momentum': checkins_7d/7 - (checkins_30d-checkins_7d)/23,\n","                         'pt_sessions_30d': int(recent_events.event_type.eq('pt_session').sum()),\n","                         'days_since_pt_purchase': (member.decision_time-member.last_pt_purchase_at).total_seconds()/86400 if pd.notna(member.last_pt_purchase_at) else np.nan,\n","                         'member_id': member.member_id,\n","                         'tenure_days': (member.decision_time - member.signup_at).days,\n","                         'checkins_30d': int(recent_events.event_type.eq('checkin').sum()),\n","                         'classes_30d': int(recent_events.event_type.eq('group_class').sum()),\n","                         'app_views_30d': int(recent_events.event_type.eq('app_view').sum()),\n","                         'days_since_checkin': (member.decision_time - checkins.event_time.max()).total_seconds()/86400 if len(checkins) else np.nan,\n","                         'inquiry_60d': int(len(enquiries) > 0)})\n","    if number % 500 == 0 or number == len(entered_observations):\n","        print(f'[INFO] Feature construction: {number}/{len(entered_observations)} members processed')\n","\n","\n","# Attach aggregates once per member; validate guards against accidental row multiplication.\n","feature_table = entered_observations.merge(pd.DataFrame(feature_rows), on='member_id', validate='one_to_one')\n","\n","\n","# Add store/city context with a many-to-one dimension join.\n","feature_table = feature_table.merge(locations, on='location_id', how='left', validate='many_to_one')\n","assert feature_table.city.notna().all() and feature_table.member_id.is_unique\n","assert not feature_table.duplicated(['member_id', 'decision_time']).any()\n","\n","\n","# locations is a static fixture dimension; changing real-world store context requires an as-of join.\n","print(f'[CHECK] Feature/profile joins: {len(entered_observations)} input → {len(feature_table)} output; unmatched 0; duplicated member keys 0; city missingness introduced 0.')\n","\n","\n","# Save a disk handoff, including audit columns and label readiness alongside predictors.\n","feature_table.to_csv(DATA_DIR / 'member_features.csv', index=False)\n","\n","\n","# Audit one training row against its underlying known events.\n","example = feature_table.loc[feature_table.campaign_id.eq('pilot_train')].iloc[0]\n","example_known = activities.loc[activities.uid.eq(example.uid) & activities.event_time.lt(example.decision_time)\n","                                & activities.available_at.le(example.decision_time)]\n","display(example_known.sort_values('event_time').tail(6))\n","display(feature_table.loc[feature_table.member_id.eq(example.member_id), ['member_id', 'decision_time'] + FEATURE_COLUMNS])\n","\n","\n","# Verify the displayed30-day check-in feature independently from its raw event rows.\n","assert int((example_known.event_type.eq('checkin') & example_known.event_time.ge(example.decision_time-pd.Timedelta(days=30))).sum()) == example.checkins_30d"],"execution_count":null,"outputs":[],"id":"02-005"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"section":"MOD-02 — Turn known event rows into one member row"},"source":["### Takeaway — MOD-02\n","\n","**Each entered member-decision now has one auditable feature row.** Known events are aggregated before joining. The saved member_features.csv carries both historical and upcoming rows; later filtering determines which can train.\n","\n","**Before moving on:** Explain in your own words how this output supports the next step."],"id":"02-006"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"section":"MOD-03 — Reserve future periods before learning transformations"},"source":["## MOD-03 — Reserve future periods before learning transformations\n","\n","### The question\n","How will we distinguish learning from evidence on later members?\n","\n","| Group | Decision period | Complete members | Role |\n","|---|---|---:|---|\n","| **Training** | January |350 | Fit preprocessing and models; develop candidate features |\n","| **Validation** | February |150 | Compare candidates and guide development |\n","| **Later evaluation** | April |125 | Evaluate the approach finalized in notebook 03 |\n","| **Upcoming** | June |1,200 | Score using saved training state; outcomes unknown |\n","\n","![Notebook02 chronological split](attachment:02_basic_modeling_02_chronological_split.png)\n","\n","### The checks\n","1. Keep only complete labels for supervised learning.\n","2. Confirm each earlier cohort's labels mature before the next decision.\n","3. Check member identities across groups and payment coverage.\n","4. Create X_train/y_train and X_validation/y_validation.\n","\n","### What to look for\n","Read the calendar and **training feature-readiness table**. Counts350/150/125 describe the chronological groups, not a cleaning attrition funnel. Training contains 76 buyers; validation contains 37."],"attachments":{"02_basic_modeling_02_chronological_split.png":{"image/png":"